# Force LF line endings on checkout for all text files. Windows checkouts with
# core.autocrlf=true were materializing CRLF, which breaks the svelte /
# vite-plugin-svelte build (`pnpm run build` -> js_parse_error). CI runs on
# Linux so it never saw it. git auto-detects binary files and leaves them alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# FOLLOWUPS.md is an append-heavy log written by many concurrent sessions, so
# the same "## Open" region conflicts on nearly every merge/rebase/cherry-pick.
# The built-in union driver keeps BOTH sides' lines instead of writing conflict
# markers. Trade-off: two sessions adding the same entry can leave a duplicate
# (harmless, easy to prune) rather than a hard conflict.
FOLLOWUPS.md merge=union
